[x] read apply_sync's write ordering/locking before touching action-mirror sync $Prerequisite for the action-mirror VTODO swap (learn to import VTODO). apply_sync's doc comment says ordering is load-bearing - TakeAction/TakeCalendar/Converged each stage .actions + sidecar writes differently via PendingBatch. Need to actually trace this before changing what read_ics_dates reads, since a mis-sequenced change here can silently clear a real scheduled_at (mistaking 'can't find the old format' for 'calendar deleted the event'). See caldav-integration/README.md design notes 2026-07-12.$ %2026-07-13T22:48 #019f5a22-7252-7c22-8e66-96aae8692720
[x] decouple sync state from the domain model $The merge base B is a property of the sync pair, not the action. Move it to a sync-owned gitignored store (.clearhead/sync/<pair>.json, action-uuid -> field -> value): plan_sync takes a base_map param symmetric with ics_dates; scheduled_at_sync/due_date_sync come OFF Action and ActionMeta (merge_action/hydrate_actions_map shrink); apply_sync stamps B into the store; one-time seed migration reads existing sidecar _sync values in. Lands BEFORE the action-mirror VTODO swap. See README design notes 2026-07-14.$ !1 %2026-07-17T23:24 #019f5f76-c52c-7020-8dbc-c0f393cf196e
[x] align sync state with the configured plans vdir $Correct the initial decoupling: vdir is the integration boundary. Replace per-pair/caldav state with one clean merge-base store for the configured plan path; remove pair/remote/CalDAV concepts and delete all legacy sidecar migration code. Missing state gets first-sync semantics.$ !1 %2026-07-17T23:45 #019f73f2-7229-7362-83f1-a095084c1761
[x] learn to export things to VTODO format $Plans already emit VTODO+RRULE. Finish the standalone Action half by replacing action_to_vevent with action_to_vtodo. RRULE remains exclusively Plan semantics and never returns to the .actions DSL; recurring capture should write a Plan VTODO directly, then expansion materializes executable Action instances.$ %2026-07-23T00:03 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3a974ca12f85
[x] learn to import VTODO $Action-mirror VTODO swap: action_to_vevent -> action_to_vtodo; Action.id is the VTODO UID and vdir filename, with no sidecar identity map. Map STATUS (blocked -> NEEDS-ACTION plus X-CLEARHEAD-STATUS:blocked), title, description, dates, priority, contexts, and completion. VTODO with RRULE is always a Plan; VTODO without RRULE is an Action projection.$ %2026-07-23T17:17 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3abe216ea948
[x] add fields to the sync store ~ $Genericize reconcile() to reconcile<T: PartialEq + Clone> and run it independently for state, title, description, and due_date. Each merge base lives in the one configured-plans-vdir projection store, never Action/ActionMeta. One field conflict must not block the others.$ %2026-07-23T17:17 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3adcba9847ba
[x] state %2026-07-23T17:17 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3afc680d10bc
[x] due date %2026-07-23T17:17 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3b1aef80a19a
[x] title %2026-07-23T17:17 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3b3d3dbdfcce
[x] description %2026-07-23T17:17 #019f5848-c3bf-7062-a94a-3b5faede09e7
[x] migrate existing plan .ics files from VEVENT\+RRULE to VTODO\+RRULE $One-time conversion command, not a permanent dual-format read path. Run once after plan_to_event/parse_ics_file switch to VTODO; old VEVENT plan format is retired after conversion. See caldav-integration/README.md design notes 2026-07-12.$ %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f59c4-8c0b-7aa1-88b8-8ec35dee0e2d
[x] make Action UUID the VTODO identity $For ClearHead-authored standalone actions use Action.id == VTODO UID == canonical vdir filename. For calendar-authored arbitrary text UIDs, retain UID and derive Action.id deterministically with UUIDv5; remember UID only in the plans projection store so missing resources can be recreated. No charter-sidecar mirror map. Audit source_vevent/external_schedule_id so recurrence-series metadata remains only where semantically real.$ !1 %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f7455-fde8-7112-a9cc-2955902ae771
[x] import calendar-created VTODOs as actions $Create an Action in the charter selected by the VTODO resource's vdir directory. UUID UIDs remain the Action UUID; arbitrary RFC 5545 UIDs derive a deterministic UUIDv5 without rewriting UID or using a sidecar identity map. Existing Actions whose projection disappears recreate the VTODO; deletion has no lifecycle meaning.$ !1 %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f91bc-d4d8-7293-943d-ddb59f28ab84
[x] sync VTODO priority and categories bidirectionally $Map standard RFC 5545 PRIORITY and CATEGORIES independently through the same per-field three-way merge. STATUS remains the only lifecycle signal; predecessor, sequential, and charter hierarchy remain ClearHead-only.$ !2 %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f91bc-d4e7-75a2-a112-1be069c3b014
[x] align VTODO specifications and interoperability coverage $Replace stale VEVENT-authoring terminology across specs/help/comments, document import and missing-projection semantics, and cover arbitrary UIDs, transport filenames, standard fields, and unknown-property preservation.$ !2 %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f91bc-d4f1-7281-8951-bbf3c1cb6c42
[_] extract calendar sync into its own crate $Deliberately deferred after VTODO sync stabilized: the vdir projection remains cohesive inside clearhead-core and extraction would currently move code without reducing coupling. Reconsider only when a second consumer needs the boundary; any future crate must remain server-agnostic.$ %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f5f76-f52a-7251-bd29-28117bf16f47
[x] build VTODO integration ~ !1 %2026-07-23T18:51 #019f5847-e4ef-75f2-a736-831b6a828f63
[x] Canonicalize the recurrence key before the occurrence UUIDv5 $CRITICAL PATH — e2e-confirmed real (2026-07-25). expand_occurrences converts DTSTART to Local then re-emits it as a FLOATING string, dropping the UTC offset: a Jan 08:00Z master yields July occurrences whose true instant is 07:00Z (DST drift), while EXDATE/RECURRENCE-ID keep their real instant. Occurrence keys and deviation keys land in different frames and never match, so EXDATE does not skip and overrides do not bind. Fix: make occurrence generation frame-preserving (anchor the recurrence in the master's original DTSTART value-type/TZID) so canonical_occurrence_key agrees on both paths. Scratch e2e reproduces: recurring plan + EXDATE, occurrence still shows.$ !1 %2026-07-25T13:20 #019f962c-eb39-7312-9da0-b36b3a9bda90
[x] Model recurrence deviations on Plan $Read + render DONE (2026-07-25). ICSPlan carries exdates/overrides from parse; render_occurrences (expand.rs) applies them and windows per plan; From<Workspace> for DomainModel is the union (materialized wins by id); load_domain_model_with_projection is the deterministic loader. Occurrence projection is e2e-proven: clearhead read actions surfaces occurrences. REMAINING: deviation MATCHING (EXDATE skip / override overlay) does not yet fire — blocked on the frame-preservation fix in the canonicalize-key invariant. Once keys agree, apply_override/exdate skipping already work.$ !1 %2026-07-25T17:41 #019f9794-bfd5-7a63-9d5f-0948163d9537
[x] Render the windowed union of actions and projected occurrences in the views =occurrence-view $Union LANDED (2026-07-25): From<Workspace> for DomainModel renders + unions occurrences at the single lowering; CLI read path surfaces them (window from expansion_total_instances); occurrences addressable by their occurrence UUIDv5; deterministic under a fixed Projection. REMAINING: consolidate the TWO assembly sites — the union is currently assembled both in From<Workspace> and in the CLI collect_all_actions (both via the one render_occurrences primitive, so no logic dup, but two sites). collect_all_actions uses load_workspace (MarkdownCharter, for file-path/-f needs) rather than the projected model; fold these into one path so no consumer re-assembles. Also depends on the frame fix for deviated occurrences to render correctly.$ !2 %2026-07-25T17:57 #019f962c-eb51-72a3-9ab9-73b93dad5959
[x] Retire expand materialization and the upcoming file $Demolition the projection model implies. Remove expand_plans_into_actions file-writing, <charter>.upcoming.actions, and expansion_primary_instances. Occurrences are projected on the fly at load, never filed; the window collapses to a single per-plan count (expansion_total_instances). A materialized occurrence line was a second master that drifts from its RRULE; projection dissolves the drift. See README design notes 2026-07-24 cont.$ !1 %2026-07-25T20:06 #019f9794-de24-7ca3-8807-9c88f81f5a96
[x] Ingest a foreign roll-forward as occurrence completion $Invariant, and a BUILD task (needs the deviation write-model to exist first). A camp-B client (Apple Reminders etc.) completes a recurring VTODO by advancing the master DTSTART with no override. Import must recognize 'master advanced one period, no new override' as completion of the prior occurrence and record that deviation, not reinterpret it as a series reschedule. No RECURRENCE-ID/master-advance detection exists today — greenfield, not verify-only.$ !1 %2026-07-25T21:08 #019f962c-eb46-77b3-931e-1e43920e7daa
[x] Route occurrence operations to deviations, not line edits =occurrence-ops $complete/skip LANDED (2026-07-25): cancel->EXDATE, complete->completed RECURRENCE-ID override, via core write_occurrence_deviation (ics.rs) + apply_occurrence_op (plans.rs). CLI complete/cancel fall through to occurrence handling only when the query is not a materialized line (materialized wins). Handle = plan_id + external_occurrence_key stamped on each rendered occurrence. e2e-proven via the real binary. REMAINING: reschedule (needs datetime args, likely update <occurrence> --scheduled-at).$ !2 %2026-07-25T21:25 <occurrence-view #019f962d-1f07-7091-a4af-9868afc2a1aa
[x] Strip calendar-only sidecar fields $Enabled by retiring materialization. Remove ActionMeta.external_schedule_id (no materialized generated lines remain to re-link; a projected occurrence carries plan linkage inherently in memory) and PlanMeta.last_expanded (nothing expands). Leave charter.id/charter.created/ActionMeta.created — generic provenance orthogonal to calendar sync, whose own fate is a separate workspace charter's call.$ !2 %2026-07-25T21:25 #019f9794-de34-7bc0-937a-73e4df2fb3b1
[x] Round-trip stamped-occurrence completion to the master deviation $Completion is calendar-managed for every stamped occurrence, not just templated ones: completing the root writes a completed RECURRENCE-ID override on the master via write_occurrence_deviation, keyed by root id = occurrence key. Atomic (childless root) is the base case; a templated root additionally keeps its rich interior local in .actions — only the rollup bit reaches the calendar (a five-child checklist is not one VTODO STATUS). Live linkage = (plan_id, slot) stamped into PlansSyncStore at stamp time, consumed/cleared when the deviation lands (the slot key is unrecoverable from the hash id or the mutable scheduled_at). Stamped instances must NOT also flatten to standalone VTODOs (avoids foreign double-vision against the master RRULE) — exclude at the loader/sync boundary like the window-0 loader already does.$ !2 +caldav %2026-07-26T23:58 #019fa019-3dc6-7060-b744-34a7279ee420
[x] Stamp the present occurrence on the write path $LANDED 2026-07-26 (atomic, e2e-proven): the single-token generator. next_active_slot (expand.rs) + shared stage_plan_token stamp the PRESENT due slot into the plan's charter .actions, keyed by id = hash(plan UID, slot), with the (plan_id, slot) link in PlansSyncStore. Wired into apply_sync (reconcile.rs), rides its lock + PendingBatch, idempotent while a token is live, jump-forward on advance, self-heals a raw-completed token on the next sync. REMAINING: graft the template step-forest for templated plans (only the atomic childless root is stamped today); a catch-up cap is mooted by single-token + jump-forward.$ !2 +caldav %2026-07-28T00:35 #019fa019-3db7-7a13-8ae1-88937dd3ccdf
[x] Disambiguate calendar collection imports from nested action filenames $Live DAVx5 acceptance: a VTODO created in the top-level next collection imported into charters/linux/next.actions because collection-to-charter routing collided with a nested file basename. Resolve collection identity against the charter mapping, not an arbitrary matching filename, and add an end-to-end regression.$ !1 +bug,caldav %2026-08-13T14:07 #019fe4e9-da30-7a03-9625-8d77f1ebb584
[x] Make calendar collection ownership a workspace invariant =workspace-collection-ownership $Make every constructed charter carry a calculated non-optional collection path under the configured plan root; quarantine unowned vdir collections, block calendar mutation, and let doctor preview or remove them with an explicit propagation warning.$ !1 %2026-08-13T20:38 #019ffe59-e8c1-7d23-a3be-41d7a343bfb0
[x] Build the present-stamping lane (atomic and templated) =stamping-lane ~ $LANDED 2026-07-28 (atomic + templated both e2e-proven; the stamp-present child is completed & in the archive). REMAINING here: only the archived-lineage child below. DESIGN (kept for reference): the single materialized lane — the two-lane split (project atomic / stamp templated) collapses (README 2026-07-26 cont.2). On the write path a generator stamps the PRESENT due occurrence: atomic = a synthesized childless root from the master VTODO (SUMMARY->title, CATEGORIES->contexts, PRIORITY->priority, id = occurrence UUIDv5 = hash(plan UID, slot)); templated = the same root + the template step-forest grafted beneath it via parent_override in instantiate_template (graft_template_steps in reconcile.rs). Also sealed the materialized-token sync leak: plan_sync excludes occurrence tokens + their grafted subtrees (occurrence_subtree_ids). GUARDRAIL held: never materialize the future — one occurrence per plan; the next is generated on completion, RRULE read fresh.$ !2 +caldav %2026-08-31T21:23 #019fa019-079f-7681-bb22-d64ab1a9f78c
    >[x] Snapshot plan-lineage onto the archived instance at completion $The ARCHIVED half of occurrence lineage. The LIVE half LANDED 2026-07-28: the loader (hydrate_occurrence_links) restamps plan_id + external_occurrence_key onto materialized tokens from the sync store, so graphd projects cco:prescribed_by while an occurrence is live. THIS item: at crystallization (completion/archival) snapshot the SEMANTIC edge onto the archived instance — realizes plan-M at temporal position T + a human label — so it survives the plan being edited/deleted (invoice-snapshots-price-at-sale). Do NOT reverse-derive from the current RRULE. Snapshot the semantic edge, never the occurrence-id hash. End state: graphd projects coherent history over live (hydrated) + archived (snapshotted) facts.$ !3 +caldav %2026-08-31T21:23 #019fa019-3dd0-7993-bcae-c0abfbf8f60d
[x] Unwind projection from the live file (file is all-materialized) =occurrence-surface $REVERSAL of the shipped atomic lane (README 2026-07-26 cont.2). LANDED 2026-07-28: removed extend_with_projected_occurrences from From<Workspace> + both CLI read collectors, and the plumbing that only fed the union (Projection struct, load_domain_model_with_projection, without_occurrences, load_model_materialized). load_domain_model is materialized-only now; a recurring plan surfaces ONE materialized present token on read, no projected window (e2e-proven). The engine (render_occurrences/render_occurrence/next_active_slot, deviation read/write, frame fix) SURVIVES for the write-path stamper + the future calendar view. REMAINING: the re-home child below.$ !2 %2026-08-31T21:23 #019f962c-ba5a-7732-ad24-df6fceadea53
    >[x] Re-home projection to future (calendar) and past (analytics) $Projection survives only as a query concern, never a core data-model piece. Future occurrences render in a read-only calendar view; past completions surface as analytics over archive/. HARD RULE: projection must never feed an index-shape query (results resolving to file:line:col to jump to/edit) — a projected occurrence has no line, so it would break the qflist as a first-class EDITING surface. The .actions file stays all-materialized; the nvim virtual-line gymnastics are obviated because present occurrences are real lines.$ !3 %2026-08-31T21:23 <occurrence-ops #019f962d-1f15-7c23-82d5-e1c8f2a652e0
    >[x] Seal the projection to sync leak $Sync reconciles owned artifacts only; a projected occurrence has no standalone resource to reconcile and no line for apply_sync to locate. sync_calendar now loads a window-0 model (Projection::without_occurrences / ctx.load_model_materialized) so occurrences are structurally absent from plan_sync, not filtered by a fragile flag. Regression-locked in workspace_store.rs. Relates to the two-assembly-sites debt in =occurrence-view.$ %2026-07-28T17:34 #019f9bdf-bad8-7940-a77e-98be6bf8b04e
    >[x] Re-cohere graphd with the materialized model $DONE 2026-07-28. Getting-it-working: removed the dead per-action external_schedule_id projection (RDF insert.rs + JSON-LD jsonld.rs) and stripped it from actions.schema/context/example v4; kept hasExternalScheduleId on the Plan node (the VTODO UID, still valid). Taking-advantage: graphd already projects plan_id->cco:prescribed_by + external_occurrence_key, but post-unwind materialized tokens reached it with plan_id=None; core loader hydration (see lineage item) restores the live link, so graphd expresses the prescription edge with ZERO new graphd code. e2e-proven via the real graphd binary (query raw: token -> prescribed_by -> plan). graphd is a pure DomainModel projector — no sync-store/archive access of its own; the edge must arrive in the model.$ %2026-07-28T17:34 #019fa7a6-600f-7221-a7aa-7b858097fa48
    >[x] Specify recurring Action masters and projected occurrence views $DECIDED from live Thunderbird + JTX acceptance: Action hierarchy and recurrence are orthogonal. RELATED-TO expresses series parentage and never implicitly grants recurrence; every Action may independently recur, so recurring checklist children carry their own explicit RRULE while persistent children do not. Occurrences remain projections keyed by series UID + canonical recurrence key, sparse RFC 5545 deviations carry state, and views lift the series hierarchy across aligned projected slots. ClearHead may offer explicit recurrence-inheritance authoring sugar, but emitted VTODOs remain self-contained. REMAINING: specify the DSL restoration, durable deviation authority, projection/view behavior, and client degradation contract.$ !2 +caldav,interoperability %2026-08-31T21:23 #019fe57b-49e7-7a42-8c9b-36a66355192b
    >[x] Round-trip VTODO parent relationships into Action hierarchy $Live JTX Board acceptance created two standalone child VTODO resources carrying RELATED-TO;RELTYPE=PARENT:<recurring-master-UID>, with no RRULE, DTSTART, DUE, or RECURRENCE-ID. ClearHead preserved the ICS properties but imported both as flat root Actions because the domain does not resolve an Action parent through a recurring Plan UID. Define and regression-test hierarchy import/export as part of the recurring-Action model.$ !1 +caldav,interoperability %2026-08-31T21:23 #019fe5b0-8a3f-7273-8341-1ca140965c25
